# Code owners (Alex, 2026-11-10; AGENTS.md, "Landing a change"). GitHub asks the owner to
# review a pull request that changes one of these paths, so Alex sees every change where
# a mistake costs the most: CI and release workflows, release and secret scripts, the
# deploy files, entitlements, the control plane, the control link, sign-in and the
# Keychain. It replaces the `risk` check (#3040), which scored the same paths and labelled
# the PR, a score nobody acted on. The lane lands its PR as usual: `main`'s ruleset does
# not require a code owner's review. No UI path is here (#3860): that would hold every
# UI PR, where #3474 holds only a new screen, control or layout.
#
# The last matching line wins, as in .gitignore.

# CI, release and supply chain
/.github/                                  @alexec
/scripts/release*.sh                       @alexec
/scripts/*secret*                          @alexec
/deploy/                                   @alexec
*.entitlements                             @alexec

# Sign-in, tokens and the Keychain
/Go/internal/controlplane/                 @alexec
/Go/internal/controllink/                  @alexec
/Go/internal/mac/signin/                   @alexec
/Go/internal/mac/keychain_darwin.go        @alexec
/Packages/AgentsKit/Sources/AgentsKitCore/Remote/  @alexec
/App/Sources/Hosts/Lending.swift           @alexec
